cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the archived release."
title: "Disulfidptosis-associated signature in diabetic nephropathy"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and results for a computational study of disulfidptosis-related
  transcriptional programs in diabetic nephropathy. Four public transcriptomic
  datasets were integrated and a seven-gene candidate signature was derived by a
  triple-machine-learning intersection strategy with nested cross-validation,
  bootstrap optimism correction and permutation testing. Pathway specificity
  analysis showed that the signature reflects convergent actin cytoskeleton and
  oxidative stress perturbation rather than disulfidptosis pathway activation.
